	<entry key="weather.adviceTitle">What it means</entry>
	<entry key="weather.manualTitle">Conditions in the game</entry>
	<entry key="weather.manualHint">Copy them from the GT7 race screen. Saved in this browser.</entry>
	<entry key="weather.advice.rain">Rain: use wet or intermediate tyres, brake earlier and keep the inputs smooth. Kerbs and painted lines have almost no grip.</entry>
	<entry key="weather.advice.damp">Damp track: the racing line dries first. Avoid kerbs and keep the tyres on the dry line.</entry>
	<entry key="weather.advice.hotTrack">Hot track: tyres overheat quickly, the rears first. Soft tyres degrade faster; manage wheelspin on exits.</entry>
	<entry key="weather.advice.coldTrack">Cold track: tyres need longer to reach their window. Expect less grip on the first laps and after a pit stop.</entry>
	<entry key="weather.advice.warming">The track is heating up: grip drops a little and tyre wear grows. Lap times may drift up.</entry>
	<entry key="weather.advice.cooling">The track is cooling down: grip improves, but tyres may fall below their window on long straights.</entry>
	<entry key="weather.advice.wind">Strong wind: braking points move with a headwind or tailwind, and fast corners feel different lap to lap.</entry>
	<entry key="weather.advice.stable">Stable, dry conditions: nothing changes the plan.</entry>
