	<entry key="setup.howTitle">How it works</entry>
	<entry key="setup.howText">Balance compares how much you steer with how much the car actually turns (lateral G and speed). Locking and wheelspin come from wheel speed against car speed, bottoming from the suspension resting at its lowest point at speed, tyre balance from front and rear temperatures. These are rules of thumb, not a simulation: your feel in the car wins.</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.entryUndersteer.title">Understeer on entry</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.entryUndersteer.why">The front washes wide while you brake and turn in.</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.midUndersteer.title">Understeer mid-corner</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.midUndersteer.why">At the apex the car needs more lock than the corner asks for.</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.exitUndersteer.title">Understeer on exit</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.exitUndersteer.why">On power the car runs wide: a tight differential pushes it straight.</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.entryOversteer.title">Oversteer on entry</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.entryOversteer.why">The rear steps out under braking.</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.midOversteer.title">Oversteer mid-corner</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.midOversteer.why">The rear lets go at the apex.</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.exitOversteer.title">Oversteer on exit</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.exitOversteer.why">The rear slides on power and you catch it with counter-steer.</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.frontLocking.title">Front wheels lock</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.frontLocking.why">The front wheels slow down faster than the car under heavy braking.</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.rearLocking.title">Rear wheels lock</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.rearLocking.why">The rear wheels lock under braking, which makes the car unstable.</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.rearWheelspin.title">Rear wheelspin</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.rearWheelspin.why">The rear wheels spin faster than the car on throttle.</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.frontWheelspin.title">Front wheelspin</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.frontWheelspin.why">The front wheels spin on throttle (front or all-wheel drive).</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.bottomingFront.title">Front bottoming out</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.bottomingFront.why">At speed the front suspension often sits at its lowest point.</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.bottomingRear.title">Rear bottoming out</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.bottomingRear.why">At speed the rear suspension often sits at its lowest point.</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.frontTyresHot.title">Front tyres work harder</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.frontTyresHot.why">The fronts run much hotter than the rears: they slide more.</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.rearTyresHot.title">Rear tyres work harder</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.rearTyresHot.why">The rears run much hotter than the fronts: they slide more.</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.tyresCold.title">Tyres below their window</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.tyresCold.why">The tyres do not reach their working temperature: try a softer compound, or check the track temperature on the Weather tab.</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.tyresOverheat.title">Tyres above their window</entry>
	<entry key="setup.advice.tyresOverheat.why">The tyres run too hot: try a harder compound and less wheelspin and sliding.</entry>
